Helios vkd3d-proton fork: the engine on NVK on RM (D3D12 on NVK)

Conduit guest/windows/docs/dxvk-on-nvk.md, stage S5. Applied to
third_party/vkd3d-proton after 0001 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

- helios_vkd3d_create_device_icd(luid, icd_gipa, iid, device): the native
  device created directly on an ICD the UMD loaded itself (NVK's
  vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr, no Vulkan loader; layer enumeration answered
  "none"), marked as running on NVK on RM (d3d12_device.helios_nvk).
- On NVK a VKD3D_HEAP_FLAG_HELIOS_VENUS_EXPORT allocation chains Conduit's
  helios_export_memory_resource_info (sType 1000384003) instead of an
  OPAQUE_FD export, and the image/buffer declares no external handle type:
  NVK then allocates the dedicated memory standalone and uncompressed and
  the UMD asks it for a KMD resource id (IMPORT_RM).
- On NVK the queue execution stream is a local timeline semaphore (ctx 0,
  cookie 0; no producer interface, no KMD stream);
  helios_vkd3d_wait_execution(queue, value, timeout) waits on it.
- Native admission accepts FL 12_0 (NVK has no ROVs, so no FL 12_1).
- helios_vkd3d.def (the retired dynamic arm, kept for engine gates) exports
  the S5 entry points, for tools/d3d12_nvk_engine.cpp.

